  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Bangladesh RRNRP: Contribution to IOM to enhanced Resilience of Rohingya Refugees WASH (joint funding with KSA)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Joint funding with the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia (KSA) - The IOM WASH program aims to improve access to adequate and equitable sanitation, and hygiene promotion for the Rohingya refugees, through sustainable WASH systems, community engagement, and emergency preparedness. This second FCDO grant will complement the ongoing FCDO project (June 2025 to March 2026). As such, it has been designed to address the additional infrastructure and NFI gaps in IOM camps, including soap to cover gaps in other camps under the area of responsibility of UNHCR and UNICEF.  The rest of the funding will be used to cover infrastructure needs in IOM camps (that the ongoing FCDO project was unable to address) such as upgrading decentralized wastewater treatment systems (DEWATS) and latrines, to enhance sanitation and hygiene conditions, alongside improving existing Material Recovery Facilities (MRFs) and solid waste segregation sites for better waste management.</narrative>
  </description>
